9. UNIVERSAL CALLER IDENTIFICATION ENGINE

Build a modular provider architecture.

Each lookup provider must be independently configurable, replaceable, testable and disableable.

The provider interface should support:

- Availability checking.
- Number lookup.
- Caller-name retrieval.
- Business-name retrieval.
- Spam reputation.
- Geographic metadata.
- Source identification.
- Confidence metadata.
- Cache policy.
- Request timeout.
- Rate limiting.
- Authentication configuration.
- Error handling.

Implement:

- Parallel provider lookups.
- Sequential fallback.
- Configurable provider priority.
- Intelligent caching.
- Duplicate request prevention.
- Result deduplication.
- Name normalization.
- Conflicting identity detection.
- Source reliability scoring.
- Stale-record detection.
- Circuit breakers.
- Automatic recovery from unavailable providers.

Show caller identification results as soon as useful information becomes available.

Update the displayed identity when additional reliable information arrives.

Never fabricate a caller name when no provider returns one.

Display unknown callers as unknown.

Clearly distinguish verified identities, community reports, inferred metadata and unverified names.

